<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>

<!--
  Stage 40: data-plane cross-JVM backend wiring scaffold. Documents how a deployment
  injects SysDaoMessageService (DB) or PulsarMessageService as the data-plane transport,
  and how the matching IDataPlaneWireCodec is selected so StreamMessageEnvelope traffic
  genuinely traverses the real backend (not LocalMessageService in-memory direct).

  Wiring architecture (Phase 1 Decision):

    * Backend selection is a DEPLOYMENT choice. nop-stream-runtime deliberately has NO
      hard dependency on nop-sys-dao / nop-message-pulsar (vision §三 constraint 8:
      platform integration priority, no self-built infra). The application layer wires
      the concrete IMessageService backend + selects the matching codec.

    * The data plane and the Stage 39 control-plane RPC SHARE one IMessageService
      instance (topic-addressed, disjoint topics: nop-stream.rpc.* for control,
      nop-stream.{jobId}.{edge}.{s}.{t} for data). Only the data-plane view is wrapped
      by DataPlaneMessageServiceAdapter (applied inside the dispatchers); the control
      plane keeps the raw service, so the two planes never mangle each other.

    * Codec selection (why a codec is needed):
        - LocalMessageService carries the envelope object by reference -> IdentityWireCodec.
        - SysDaoMessageService persists only an ApiRequest's data field; a bare envelope
          loses its body -> SysDaoWireCodec wraps envelope as ApiRequest{data: envelopeMap}.
        - PulsarMessageService (Schema.STRING) needs a String value -> PulsarStringWireCodec
          serializes the envelope to a JSON String.
      The codecs live in nop-stream-runtime (main) and reference only ApiRequest/ApiMessage/
      JsonTool — they do NOT import the backend classes, so no backend dependency is introduced.

  This file is the Stage 42 multi-JVM deployment scaffold. TestDataPlaneSysDaoBackendE2E /
  TestDataPlanePulsarBackendE2E exercise the documented wiring programmatically (real
  H2-backed SysDaoMessageService / real PulsarMessageService), proving the scaffold is
  non-hollow (plan guide #11/#24).

  Deployment template (illustrative — concrete bean ids depend on the app assembly):

    <bean id="streamMessageService"
          class="io.nop.sys.dao.message.SysDaoMessageService">
        <property name="daoProvider" ref="nopDaoProvider"/>
    </bean>

    <bean id="streamDistributedExecutor"
          class="io.nop.stream.runtime.execution.RpcDistributedExecutor">
        <property name="messageService" ref="streamMessageService"/>
        <property name="dataPlaneWireCodec"
                  class="io.nop.stream.runtime.transport.SysDaoWireCodec"
                  ioc:bean="true"/>
    </bean>

  Pulsar variant: wire io.nop.message.pulsar.PulsarMessageService as streamMessageService
  (with its PulsarClientConfig + init/destroy lifecycle) and set dataPlaneWireCodec to
  io.nop.stream.runtime.transport.PulsarStringWireCodec.
-->
<beans x:schema="/nop/schema/beans.xdef" xmlns:x="/nop/schema/xdsl.xdef"
       xmlns:ioc="ioc" xmlns:feature="feature">

    <!--
      Default in-process transport. ioc:default yields to an explicitly-wired
      IMessageService of the same id (the app wires SysDaoMessageService /
      PulsarMessageService for cross-JVM). Mirrors stream-control-rpc.beans.xml so the
      control and data planes share one transport bean when deployed together.
    -->
    <bean id="streamMessageService" ioc:default="true"
          class="io.nop.message.core.local.LocalMessageService"/>

    <!--
      Default data-plane codec: identity (matches the default LocalMessageService above).
      A deployment overrides this with SysDaoWireCodec / PulsarStringWireCodec to match
      its chosen backend.
    -->
    <bean id="streamDataPlaneWireCodec" ioc:default="true"
          class="io.nop.stream.runtime.transport.IdentityWireCodec"/>

</beans>
